\title{Sets of characters are read without lists of their entries}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-17}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1057}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|CharSet~} no longer builds a list of its entries to be read. The equality of two sets reads both in step through the iterator of \code{\verb~|WavlMap~} and is about three times faster for sets of 2,000 stretches; \code{\verb~|spans~} is a third faster; union, intersection and difference gain a few percent. \code{\verb~|CharSet::iter~} is new and yields the stretches in order, one at a time; the UTF-8 translation reads a set through it. See [the measurements](design-wavl-walker-regex).}

\p{In review as \pr{1057}.}
